    "body": "# Problem:\r\n   Virtual lines with `virt_lines_overflow='wrap'` split words at the\r\n   viewport boundary even when 'linebreak' is enabled. The same issue\r\n   affects 'auto' when 'wrap' is enabled.\r\n\r\n   Solution:\r\n   Respect 'breakat' boundaries when laying out wrapped virtual lines.\r\n   Pass the resulting row end offsets to the renderer so it stops\r\n   drawing text at the same boundaries while preserving EOL highlights.\r\n\r\n   Fixes #41369.\r\n# Tests:\r\n  - Add coverage for linebreak, custom breakat, wrap/auto modes,\r\n    highlight chunks, EOL highlights, indentation, long words,\r\n    tabs, wide characters, resizing and scrolling.\r\n  - decorations_spec.lua: 199 passed, 1 existing skipped test.\r\n  - listlbr_spec.lua: 5 passed.\r\n  - listlbr_utf8_spec.lua: 3 passed.\r\n\r\n# AI disclosure:\r\n   AI assistance was used for codebase guidance, regression tests,\r\n   and some code comments.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-17T04:44:49Z",
